			"color":"#2a363b",
			"widgets_values":[
				"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Cinematic realistic Chinese-animation style, dark xianxia epic, 16:9, a fresh 18mm high side-rear ultra-wide keeps continuity — same altitude, same sword sect below, same storm tone, same crimson silk scale, remaining demon tide still dense on the ground; the camera pulls back and up as the senior disciple holds position on one raised palm, the silk-like energy layering into a vast staggered sky curtain, no new swords yet. [Shot 2] At 00:01.500, the camera travels up along the silk toward the far sky: silver points arrive continuously from cloud banks, both horizons, distant ridges and high depths, converging; a high oblique ultra-wide shows the incoming streams braiding into an irregular three-dimensional vortex tide above him — outer layer circling, middle layer slanting in, inner layer twisting, tributaries splitting and merging — the figure stable at its center, robe and scarf streaming. [Shot 3] At 00:04.100, a 50mm side-front shot pushes into a 75mm extreme close-up of his eyes as he lifts his head; the dutch tilt straightens exactly at the moment his eyes open; ambient sound drops for a beat — a single clear trigger; lightning ignites in his pupils. [Shot 4] At 00:04.900, a match cut from the eye-light back to the 18mm ultra-wide: silk flares outward, the vortex tide swells, crimson lightning traces light up across thousands of blades, the battlefield falls into shadow and a ring-shaped compression wave rolls out through the air — heaven and earth starting in one instant; a 35mm medium shows him giving one horizontal wave of his hand, a silk command line running through the tide, twisting motion converting into unified forward drive. [Shot 5] At 00:06.000, pulled-back lateral wide shots track the sword tide crossing the sky; over the demon tide its head dives, the middle bends into a vertical arc face, the tail follows late, folding into eight to twelve sky-hanging falls; fast alternation of high oblique and low ground-level lateral views shows tens of thousands of normal-sized silver swords covering foreground, center, wings and rear in layered depths, most of the tide annihilated while a connected network of sword-fall marks and gouges scars the ground. [Shot 6] At 00:08.400, crimson lightning spreads only along those fall points, demon-body rents and trenches, linking into a ground grid; the low-altitude surviving swords re-form into a dense heavy current and, riding a ground-hugging red silk layer, sweep sideways as a thunder-sword tsunami through the last pockets; in the core the linked lightning grid destabilizes — a ring shockwave, tearing strata, black-red volumetric blast clouds, debris and silk energy expanding outward in a final annihilation bloom, the figure still hovering high above, the wave still running outward in the final frame.\n\noverall_soundscape: Rising wind through the gathering vortex, a brief near-silence at the eye-open trigger, then the unified roar of the whole sky-tide driving forward, layered sword-waterfall impacts, crackling ground lightning networks, the tearing boom of the ring shockwave and rolling strata rupture. No dialogue, no music.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A\n"
			],
